RabuShinAIGM Privacy Policy

Effective Date: August 29, 2026
Last Updated: August 29, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how RabuShinAIGM ("RabuShinAIGM," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, stores, shares, and protects information when you use the RabuShinAIGM Discord application and related services.

By using RabuShinAIGM, you acknowledge the practices described in this Privacy Policy.

1. Information We Collect

The information RabuShinAIGM processes depends on the features you use.

Discord Information

When you interact with RabuShinAIGM through Discord, we may receive information made available by Discord that is necessary to operate the application, including:

Discord user ID;
Discord username;
display name or server nickname;
server or interaction identifiers where necessary;
campaign membership information; and
information associated with your interaction with the application.

We do not intentionally collect unrelated Discord conversations that are not provided to or required by RabuShinAIGM.

Campaign Information

RabuShinAIGM may store information associated with campaigns you create or join, including:

campaign ID;
campaign name;
campaign join code;
campaign owner;
campaign membership;
campaign state;
world state;
encounter state;
multiplayer synchronization information; and
campaign progress.
Character Information

RabuShinAIGM may store information you create for game characters, including:

character name;
species or race;
class;
level;
background;
ability scores;
hit points;
armor class;
inventory;
equipment;
currency;
spells;
spell slots or similar resources;
abilities and features;
conditions;
character description;
backstory;
notes;
character portrait; and
other tabletop gameplay information.
Campaign Communications

When communication features are used, RabuShinAIGM may process or store:

campaign chat;
party chat;
actions submitted during gameplay;
journal content;
player notes;
messages sent to the AI Game Master; and
AI Game Master responses.

Information shared in multiplayer campaign areas may be visible to other members of that campaign.

AI Game Master Information

When you use AI Game Master features, information necessary to generate a response may be transmitted to an AI service provider such as OpenAI.

Depending on the context of the request, this may include:

your submitted action;
recent campaign conversation;
character information;
party information;
current location;
encounter or combat state;
game rules or instructions;
relevant campaign history; and
other information necessary for the AI Game Master to respond appropriately.

Do not include sensitive personal information in AI Game Master prompts unless necessary.

Technical and Operational Information

We may process limited technical information necessary to operate, troubleshoot, and protect the Service, such as:

application errors;
timestamps;
synchronization status;
request status;
application version;
multiplayer connection information;
diagnostic information; and
security-related events.

Where practical, diagnostic information is designed to avoid unnecessary personal information.

2. Information We Do Not Intentionally Collect

RabuShinAIGM is not designed to intentionally collect:

government identification numbers;
financial-account passwords;
credit-card information;
medical records;
precise GPS location;
biometric identifiers; or
unrelated private Discord messages.

Users should not submit this type of information through campaign chat, character information, journals, or AI Game Master prompts.

3. OpenAI API Credentials

If RabuShinAIGM allows you to provide your own OpenAI API key, that credential is used only to authenticate requests made using your OpenAI API account.

Your API key should not be included in campaign chat or exposed to other players.

Where RabuShinAIGM stores an API credential locally, it should be protected using the security mechanisms implemented by the application.

RabuShinAIGM does not intentionally share one user's private API key with another campaign participant.

Users are responsible for maintaining the security and billing status of their own OpenAI API account.

4. How We Use Information

We use information processed through RabuShinAIGM to:

create and maintain user sessions;
identify users interacting with the application;
create and manage campaigns;
allow users to join multiplayer campaigns;
save characters and character progress;
synchronize multiplayer game information;
provide campaign chat;
maintain combat and encounter state;
generate AI Game Master responses;
maintain journals and campaign history;
display appropriate game information;
prevent unauthorized campaign access;
detect abuse or security issues;
troubleshoot errors;
maintain and improve the Service; and
comply with applicable legal obligations.

We do not sell personal information for monetary compensation.

5. AI Processing

When AI Game Master features are used, relevant game information is sent to the configured AI provider so that it can generate a response.

For OpenAI-powered features, prompts and responses are processed according to OpenAI's applicable terms, privacy policies, and API data practices.

OpenAI currently states that API inputs and outputs are not used to train its models by default unless the API customer explicitly opts into applicable data-sharing programs. Users should review OpenAI's current policies because provider practices may change.

6. How Information Is Shared

We do not sell RabuShinAIGM user data to advertisers.

Information may be disclosed in the following situations.

Other Campaign Participants

Multiplayer campaign members may receive information necessary for shared gameplay, including:

character information;
character portraits;
game actions;
campaign chat;
party information;
combat state;
dice results; and
AI Game Master responses.
Discord

Information transmitted through Discord remains subject to Discord's systems and policies.

Discord may process information relating to application interactions as part of operating its platform.

Supabase

RabuShinAIGM may use Supabase for database, authentication, synchronization, realtime, storage, or related backend services.

Information necessary for those services may therefore be processed by Supabase.

Supabase describes database and other backend services that may store and process application customer data and provides security mechanisms including Row Level Security.

OpenAI

Relevant prompts and game information may be transmitted to OpenAI when OpenAI-powered AI Game Master features are used.

Hosting and Infrastructure Providers

Information may be processed by the hosting, networking, database, logging, or infrastructure provider used to operate production RabuShinAIGM services.

The specific provider may change as the Service develops.

Legal or Security Requirements

Information may be disclosed where reasonably necessary to:

comply with applicable law;
respond to valid legal process;
investigate fraud or abuse;
protect users;
protect the security of RabuShinAIGM; or
protect legal rights.
7. Data Retention

We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, operation of active campaigns, security, dispute resolution, legal obligations, backups, and legitimate operational purposes.

Campaign information may remain stored while a campaign remains active.

Information may remain temporarily in backups after deletion from active systems.

We may establish more specific retention periods as the production infrastructure develops.

